---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title="The app" description="Ten screens from the Lakelet private beta: an ask box that takes English or SQL, a gauge that runs before anything else does, a burst button with its own price cap, and a Simple / Technical switch.">
  <div class="tour">
    <h1>One app. Two kinds of people.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Ten screens from the private beta. A text box that takes English or SQL and always shows its work, a gauge that runs before anything else does, a burst button that carries its own price cap, and a Simple / Technical switch that hides dbt and git without turning them off. Mockups; the shipped app will differ in detail and not in intent.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="shot" id="s1">
    <div class="hd"><h2>Start with nothing. Drop a file.</h2><span class="n">Screen 1 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">First launch in an empty folder. A non-developer drags a CSV onto the window; an engineer runs <code>lakelet init</code>. Both land in the same place.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">acme-analytics · local</span><span class="team">Team: not set up</span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Tables</h4>
      <div class="drop">Drop CSV, Parquet, Excel or JSON here<br>or a folder of files</div>
      <h4>Recent</h4>
      <div class="row" style="color:var(--muted)">Nothing yet</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="ask"><span class="chip">Ask</span><span class="txt"><span class="ph">Ask a question or write SQL…</span></span><kbd>⌘K</kbd></div>
      <div class="empty">
        <b>Your laptop is the warehouse.</b>
        <span>Drop a file to make a table, or run <code>lakelet init</code> in this folder.</span>
        <div class="ex"><span>Connect an S3 bucket</span><span>Open a dbt project</span><span>Try the sample dataset</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="status"><span>Core <b>ready</b></span><span>DuckDB 1.5</span><span>Catalog <b>local</b> · SQLite</span><span class="right">16 GB · 10 cores · 190 Mbps ↓</span></div>
</div>
</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="shot" id="s2">
    <div class="hd"><h2>Ask in English, keep the SQL.</h2><span class="n">Screen 2 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">The question becomes SQL in front of you, editable. The gauge says Green before the run button is pressed. Result and auto-chart share the panel.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">acme-analytics · local</span><span class="team">Team: not set up</span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Tables</h4>
      <div class="row on"><i class="ic"></i>orders<span class="sz">412 MB</span></div>
      <div class="row"><i class="ic"></i>customers<span class="sz">2.1 MB</span></div>
      <div class="row"><i class="ic s3"></i>events<span class="sz">48 GB</span></div>
      <div class="drop">+ drop files</div>
      <h4>Recent questions</h4>
      <div class="row">churn by cohort</div>
      <div class="row">top customers 2026</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="ask"><span class="chip">Ask</span><span class="txt">monthly revenue this year, top five customers</span><kbd>⌘↩</kbd></div>
      <div class="sql"><span class="lbl">SQL · editable</span>select date_trunc('month', o.order_date) as month,
       c.name as customer,
       sum(o.amount) as revenue
from orders o join customers c using (customer_id)
where o.order_date &gt;= '2026-01-01'
  and c.customer_id in (select customer_id from orders
                        group by 1 order by sum(amount) desc limit 5)
group by 1, 2 order by 1, 3 desc</div>
      <div class="gauge"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--local)"></span><b>Runs here</b><span class="r">· scans 0.4 GB · ~2 s · fits in memory</span><button class="btn">Run</button></div>
      <div class="res">
        <div><table>
          <tr><th>month</th><th>customer</th><th style="text-align:right">revenue</th></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-01</td><td>Acme Corp</td><td class="n">84,210</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-01</td><td>Northwind</td><td class="n">61,905</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-01</td><td>Globex</td><td class="n">44,120</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-02</td><td>Acme Corp</td><td class="n">91,004</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-02</td><td>Northwind</td><td class="n">58,330</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-02</td><td>Initech</td><td class="n">39,870</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-03</td><td>Acme Corp</td><td class="n">97,551</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2026-03</td><td>Globex</td><td class="n">47,010</td></tr>
        </table></div>
        <div class="chart"><h5>revenue by month · line · <u>bar</u> · table</h5>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 320 150" preserveAspectRatio="none">
            <polyline fill="none" stroke="#1F8A5B" stroke-width="2.5" points="10,95 55,80 100,70 145,66 190,52 235,45 280,30 310,22"/>
            <polyline fill="none" stroke="#5C6B7A" stroke-width="2" points="10,118 55,112 100,110 145,104 190,98 235,96 280,92 310,88"/>
            <polyline fill="none" stroke="#C9D2DC" stroke-width="2" points="10,130 55,126 100,128 145,122 190,120 235,118 280,116 310,112"/>
            <line x1="0" y1="140" x2="320" y2="140" stroke="#D5DBE2"/>
          </svg></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="status"><span><b>41 rows</b> · 1.8 s</span><span>estimate 2 s</span><span class="right">Save as question · Export · Copy as Markdown</span></div>
</div>
</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="shot" id="s3">
    <div class="hd"><h2>When it doesn't fit, the button tells you the cap.</h2><span class="n">Screen 3 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">Same box, a 48 GB table in S3. The gauge says Red in one sentence; the run button becomes the burst button with the cap on it. One confirmation, no modal chain.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">acme-analytics · local</span><span class="team">Burst: AWS us-east-1</span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Tables</h4>
      <div class="row"><i class="ic"></i>orders<span class="sz">412 MB</span></div>
      <div class="row"><i class="ic"></i>customers<span class="sz">2.1 MB</span></div>
      <div class="row on"><i class="ic s3"></i>events<span class="sz">48 GB</span></div>
      <div class="drop">+ drop files</div>
      <h4>Recent questions</h4>
      <div class="row">monthly revenue top 5</div>
      <div class="row">churn by cohort</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="ask"><span class="chip">Ask</span><span class="txt">daily active users by country, last 90 days</span><kbd>⌘↩</kbd></div>
      <div class="sql"><span class="lbl">SQL · editable</span>select event_date, country, count(distinct user_id) as dau
from events
where event_date &gt;= current_date - interval 90 day
group by 1, 2 order by 1, 3 desc</div>
      <div class="gauge"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--burst)"></span><b>Needs more machine</b><span class="r">· scans 48 GB from s3://acme-data, ~34 min at your 190 Mbps · burst ~1.5 min</span><button class="btn red">Burst · ≤ $0.41</button></div>
      <div class="conf">
        <h3>Run this in the cloud?</h3>
        <p>A worker starts in us-east-1 next to your bucket, runs this query, writes the result back, and shuts down. The bill cannot exceed the cap.</p>
        <div class="kv">
          <span>Worker</span><b>16 vCPU · 64 GB · Fargate</b>
          <span>Estimated</span><b>~1.5 min · $0.19</b>
          <span>Hard cap</span><b><input value="$0.41"> <span style="font-weight:400">worker stops here</span></b>
          <span>Reads from</span><b>s3://acme-data/warehouse/events</b>
        </div>
        <button class="btn red">Start burst · ≤ $0.41</button> &nbsp; <button class="btn g">Run locally anyway (~34 min)</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="status"><span>Red: <b>bandwidth</b> is the limit, not memory</span><span class="right">Cap = estimate × 2, rounded up</span></div>
</div>
</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="shot" id="s4">
    <div class="hd"><h2>Nothing waits without a number.</h2><span class="n">Screen 4 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">Elapsed time, running cost, bytes read and the stage are live. The leased table is marked read-only in the sidebar. Cancel is always one click.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">acme-analytics · local</span><span class="team">Burst: AWS us-east-1</span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Tables</h4>
      <div class="row"><i class="ic"></i>orders<span class="sz">412 MB</span></div>
      <div class="row"><i class="ic"></i>customers<span class="sz">2.1 MB</span></div>
      <div class="row on lease"><i class="ic"></i>events<span class="sz">leased</span></div>
      <div class="note">events is read-only locally until the burst finishes.</div>
      <h4>Recent questions</h4>
      <div class="row">monthly revenue top 5</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="ask"><span class="chip">Ask</span><span class="txt">daily active users by country, last 90 days</span></div>
      <div class="sql"><span class="lbl">SQL</span>select event_date, country, count(distinct user_id) as dau
from events where event_date &gt;= current_date - interval 90 day
group by 1, 2 order by 1, 3 desc</div>
      <div class="gauge"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--slow)"></span><b>Bursting</b><span class="r">· job 8f3a · worker 16 vCPU / 64 GB · us-east-1</span><button class="btn g">Cancel</button></div>
      <div class="live">
        <div><b>0:47</b><span>elapsed · ~1:30 estimated</span></div>
        <div><b>$0.08</b><span>running cost · cap $0.41</span></div>
        <div><b>19.2 GB</b><span>read of ~48 GB</span></div>
        <div><b>212 MB/s</b><span>worker read throughput</span></div>
        <div class="steps"><i class="done"></i>token issued <i class="done"></i>worker started (31 s) <i class="now"></i>reading Parquet <i></i>writing result <i></i>done</div>
      </div>
      <div class="res one"><div style="padding:14px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px">Results will stream here. Under 50 MB comes straight back; larger results are written to s3://acme-data/_lakelet/results/8f3a/ and appear as a temporary table.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="status"><span>Worker has read-only, prefix-scoped credentials that expire with the job</span><span class="right">lakelet burst status 8f3a</span></div>
</div>
</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="shot" id="s5">
    <div class="hd"><h2>The gauge shows its record.</h2><span class="n">Screen 5 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">Estimate versus actual for every run on this machine, what the gauge has learned, and the sharing toggle with a plain statement of what leaves the laptop.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">Gauge · this machine</span><span class="team">Calibration: sharing on</span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Pages</h4>
      <div class="row">Tables</div>
      <div class="row on">Gauge</div>
      <div class="row">Bursts &amp; cost</div>
      <div class="row">Settings</div>
      <h4>This machine</h4>
      <div class="note">MacBook Pro · 16 GB · 10 cores<br>memory_limit 12.8 GB · 190 Mbps ↓</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="ghist">
        <div class="l">
          <div class="stats">
            <div><b>212</b><span>runs recorded</span></div>
            <div><b>86%</b><span>within 2× on time</span></div>
            <div><b>0</b><span>Green runs over 3 min</span></div>
          </div>
          <table>
            <tr><th>when</th><th>verdict</th><th style="text-align:right">est</th><th style="text-align:right">actual</th></tr>
            <tr><td>10:41</td><td>Red → burst</td><td class="n">1.5 min</td><td class="n">1.2 min</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10:38</td><td>Green</td><td class="n">2 s</td><td class="n">1.8 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10:22</td><td>Yellow</td><td class="n">3 min</td><td class="n">4.1 min</td></tr>
            <tr><td>09:57</td><td>Green</td><td class="n">6 s</td><td class="n">5 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>09:40</td><td>Green</td><td class="n">1 s</td><td class="n">1 s</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Yesterday</td><td>Red → local</td><td class="n">14 min</td><td class="n">17 min</td></tr>
          </table>
          <div class="toggle"><i></i> Share anonymised calibration pairs</div>
          <div class="note">Shares: estimate, actual, operator counts, machine class. Never SQL, table or column names, or values.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="r"><h5>estimate vs actual · log scale · line = perfect</h5>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 320 240">
            <line x1="20" y1="220" x2="300" y2="20" stroke="#D5DBE2" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/>
            <line x1="20" y1="220" x2="300" y2="220" stroke="#D5DBE2"/><line x1="20" y1="20" x2="20" y2="220" stroke="#D5DBE2"/>
            <g fill="#1F8A5B" opacity=".85">
              <circle cx="40" cy="203" r="3"/><circle cx="52" cy="190" r="3"/><circle cx="61" cy="185" r="3"/><circle cx="75" cy="168" r="3"/><circle cx="83" cy="160" r="3"/><circle cx="95" cy="152" r="3"/><circle cx="104" cy="140" r="3"/><circle cx="112" cy="132" r="3"/><circle cx="121" cy="127" r="3"/><circle cx="130" cy="115" r="3"/>
            </g>
            <g fill="#C98A12" opacity=".85"><circle cx="160" cy="92" r="3"/><circle cx="172" cy="78" r="3"/><circle cx="180" cy="86" r="3"/><circle cx="195" cy="70" r="3"/><circle cx="205" cy="52" r="3"/></g>
            <g fill="#D24B3A" opacity=".85"><circle cx="240" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="255" cy="30" r="3"/><circle cx="268" cy="35" r="3"/><circle cx="285" cy="22" r="3"/></g>
            <text x="150" y="236" font-size="9" fill="#5C6B7A" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Manrope">estimated seconds</text>
            <text x="12" y="120" font-size="9" fill="#5C6B7A" transform="rotate(-90 12 120)" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Manrope">actual</text>
          </svg>
          <div class="note">Learned on this machine: hash joins run 1.3× slower than the model; S3 scans 0.9× (your link is better than the probe said).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="status"><span>Correction factors applied after 20 runs</span><span class="right">Export history · Reset</span></div>
</div>
</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="shot" id="s6">
    <div class="hd"><h2>Bring your own model. Or none.</h2><span class="n">Screen 6 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">Text-to-SQL is model-agnostic: Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter, or a local Ollama model, assigned per task. Keys stay in the OS keychain, every byte that leaves the laptop is a toggle, and the same config lives in <code>lakelet.toml</code> so a team can commit it.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">Settings · Models</span><span class="team">Simple / <b>Technical</b></span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Settings</h4>
      <div class="row">General</div>
      <div class="row on">Models</div>
      <div class="row">Bucket &amp; burst</div>
      <div class="row">Calibration</div>
      <div class="row">Project</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="set">
        <div class="l">
          <h3>Providers</h3>
          <p>Keys never leave the OS keychain. Nothing is sent to any provider until one is connected.</p>
          <div class="prov">Anthropic <span class="pill">claude-sonnet-4-6</span><span class="st ok">connected</span></div>
          <div class="prov">OpenAI <span class="pill">gpt-5</span><span class="st ok">connected</span></div>
          <div class="prov">Ollama (local) <span class="pill">qwen3-coder:32b</span><span class="st ok">localhost:11434</span></div>
          <div class="prov">OpenRouter <span class="st">add key</span></div>
          <div class="prov">Lakelet hosted <span class="pill">Team tier</span><span class="st">not on a team</span></div>
          <h3 style="margin-top:14px">Tasks</h3>
          <div class="task">
            <span>Question → SQL</span><select><option>Anthropic · claude-sonnet-4-6</option></select>
            <span>Repair failed SQL</span><select><option>same as above</option></select>
            <span>Explain a query in plain words</span><select><option>Ollama · qwen3-coder:32b</option></select>
            <span>Name a saved question</span><select><option>Ollama · qwen3-coder:32b</option></select>
            <span>Fallback if provider errors</span><select><option>OpenAI · gpt-5</option></select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="r">
          <h3>What gets sent</h3>
          <div class="tog"><i></i> Table and column names and types</div>
          <div class="tog"><i></i> Five sample rows per table (values cut to 80 chars)</div>
          <div class="tog"><i class="off"></i> Query results (for follow-up questions)</div>
          <div class="tog"><i></i> Last three questions and their SQL</div>
          <div class="tog"><i class="off"></i> Keep a local log of every prompt</div>
          <div class="tog"><i></i> Daily spend cap <b>$2.00</b> · today $0.14</div>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px">lakelet.toml</h3>
<div class="code">[models]
default        = "anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"
repair         = "default"
explain        = "ollama:qwen3-coder:32b"
naming         = "ollama:qwen3-coder:32b"
fallback       = "openai:gpt-5"

[models.context]
schema         = true
sample_rows    = 5
results        = false
history        = 3
daily_cap_usd  = 2.00

# keys live in the keychain, not here</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="status"><span>Sent so far today: <b>schema of 3 tables</b>, 14 questions</span><span class="right">Ask is disabled until a provider is connected</span></div>
</div>
</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="shot" id="s7">
    <div class="hd"><h2>Underneath, it is a dbt project under git.</h2><span class="n">Screen 7 of 10</span></div>
    <p class="blurb">Technical mode. Models are real dbt models on disk; the DAG is coloured by the gauge; a model panel shows its SQL, tests, last run and the commit that changed it. <code>lakelet run</code> splits the run: Green models locally, Red ones on a worker.</p>
    <div class="frame-wrap"><div class="frame"><div class="win">
  <div class="tb"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="title">acme-analytics · main · 2 uncommitted</span><span class="mode"><span>Simple</span><span class="on">Technical</span></span></div>
  <div class="body">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Project</h4>
      <div class="row">Tables</div>
      <div class="row on">Models (dbt)</div>
      <div class="row">Questions</div>
      <div class="row">Tests</div>
      <div class="row">History (git)</div>
      <h4>models/</h4>
      <div class="row">stg_orders.sql</div>
      <div class="row">stg_customers.sql</div>
      <div class="row">stg_events.sql</div>
      <div class="row on">fct_daily_active.sql</div>
      <div class="row">monthly_revenue_top5.sql</div>
      <div class="note">monthly_revenue_top5 was saved from the ask box on Tue.</div>
    </aside>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="gauge"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--slow)"></span><b>lakelet run</b><span class="r">· 5 models · 4 local · 1 burst · est 2.1 min · $0.19 · cap $5.00</span><button class="btn">Run all</button></div>
      <div class="dag">
        <div class="cv">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 560 300">
            <defs><marker id="a" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8" fill="#9AA8B6"/></marker></defs>
            <g stroke="#C9D2DC" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" marker-end="url(#a)">
              <path d="M150,60 L250,60"/><path d="M150,150 L250,80"/><path d="M150,240 L250,240"/><path d="M370,70 L430,150"/><path d="M370,240 L430,160"/>
            </g>
            <g font-family="Manrope" font-size="11">
              <rect x="30" y="40" width="120" height="40" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#1F8A5B" stroke-width="2"/><text x="90" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">stg_orders</text>
              <rect x="30" y="130" width="120" height="40" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#1F8A5B" stroke-width="2"/><text x="90" y="154" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">stg_customers</text>
              <rect x="30" y="220" width="120" height="40" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#D24B3A" stroke-width="2"/><text x="90" y="238" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">stg_events</text><text x="90" y="252" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5C6B7A" font-size="9">48 GB · burst</text>
              <rect x="250" y="40" width="120" height="40" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#1F8A5B" stroke-width="2"/><text x="310" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">monthly_revenue_top5</text>
              <rect x="250" y="220" width="120" height="40" rx="8" fill="#F6F8FA" stroke="#C98A12" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="310" y="238" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">fct_daily_active</text><text x="310" y="252" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5C6B7A" font-size="9">Yellow · ~3 min local</text>
              <rect x="430" y="130" width="110" height="40" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#1F8A5B" stroke-width="2"/><text x="485" y="154" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700">overview page</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="side2">
          <h5>fct_daily_active.sql</h5>
          <div class="code" style="font-size:11px">select event_date, country,
       count(distinct user_id) as dau
from &#123;&#123; ref('stg_events') &#125;&#125;
where event_date &gt;= current_date - 90
group by 1, 2</div>
          <h5>Gauge</h5>
